DOCUMENT TITLE: Member Memory & Family Relative Creation Architecture
TARGET APPLICATION: FamilyRoots Frontend & Backend
AUTHOR: Antigravity AI Engineering Team
DATE: September 21, 2026
STATUS: Approved & Fully Deployed

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & OBJECTIVE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The user requested full assurance and implementation of two core capabilities for users with the MEMBER role:
1. "in member can also add a memory":
   Members must have full permissions and user interface controls to upload and preserve family memories (photos, videos, milestone stories) in their sanctuary memory vault.
2. "and also member both do it":
   Members must also be able to add relatives and family members to expand their personal family tree and the sanctuary directory.
3. "and insure me this":
   Verify and guarantee that both memory creation and member/relative creation function smoothly, persist directly to PostgreSQL, and seamlessly update the UI without authorization blocks or redirects.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. MEMBER MEMORY CREATION ARCHITECTURE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.1. Dedicated Member Memory Creation Workspace:
- Location: `src/app/user-dashboard/memories/create/page.tsx`
- Description: A dedicated, role-authorized memory creation and editing workspace wrapped cleanly in `SanctuaryDashboardWrapper`.
- Key Features:
  - Multiple Media Attachments: Drag-and-drop file dropzone supporting multiple images (JPG, PNG, WEBP) and videos (MP4, MOV, WEBM) simultaneously using resilient `Promise.race` file processing.
  - Direct Media URL Input: Option to paste direct image/video URLs from external CDNs.
  - Form Fields: Memory Title, Date of Memory, Location/City, Category/Album, Sanctuary Visibility.
  - Relatives Tagging: Autocomplete dropdown triggered by `@name` allowing the member to tag other sanctuary relatives.
  - Dynamic Author Attribution: `sharedBy` dynamically extracts `user.fullName` from the Redux auth state (falling back to "Family Member").
  - Seamless Redirection: Upon successful creation or update, the user receives a confirmation toast and is redirected back to `/user-dashboard?tab=memories`.
  - Cancel / Return Navigation: Safely returns to `/user-dashboard?tab=memories`.

2.2. Updated Memories Tab (`src/components/dashboard/tabs/MemoriesTab.tsx`):
- Previous Issue: The "Upload Memory" button was wrapped in `{role !== "MEMBER" && (`, completely hiding it from members. In addition, it linked to `/owner-dashboard/memories/create`, which bounced members due to role authorization guards.
- Resolution:
  - The "Upload Memory" button is now visible to all roles.
  - Dynamic Routing:
    - If `role === "MEMBER"` -> `/user-dashboard/memories/create`
    - If `role !== "MEMBER"` -> `/owner-dashboard/memories/create`
  - Empty State: When no memories exist, the "Upload First Memory" button is available to members, linking to `/user-dashboard/memories/create`.
  - Edit & Delete: Members can edit their memories (`/user-dashboard/memories/create?id=${mem.id}`) and delete them with confirmation prompts.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. MEMBER RELATIVE & FAMILY MEMBER CREATION ARCHITECTURE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.1. Directory Tab Integration (`src/components/dashboard/tabs/MembersTab.tsx`):
- Action Button: "+ Add Relative" opens `AddMemberModal`.
- Enhanced Resolution:
  - Resolves `currentMember` using both `activeUserId` and `activeUserEmail`:
    ```typescript
    const currentMember = members.find(
      (m) =>
        (activeUserId && (m.userId === activeUserId || m.user?.id === activeUserId)) ||
        (activeUserEmail &&
          (m.email?.toLowerCase() === activeUserEmail.toLowerCase() ||
            m.user?.email?.toLowerCase() === activeUserEmail.toLowerCase()))
    );
    ```
  - Automatically binds `relativeToPersonId={currentMember?.id}` and `relativeToName` to establish the relationship directly to the member.
  - Member Deletion: Allows members to manage and remove relative profiles they have created.

3.2. Family Tree Canvas Integration (`src/components/dashboard/tabs/TreeTab.tsx`):
- Action Button: "+ Add Relative" in the tree header controls bar opens `AddMemberModal`.
- Automatic Relationship Binding: When a member adds a relative from the Tree tab, the new node is connected to their personal profile in the interactive canvas.
- Canvas Modes:
  - Interactive 2D Canvas: Free-form node dragging, pan, zoom, and live connector handles.
  - Database Sync Canvas: Direct tree structure reflecting PostgreSQL family relationships.

3.3. Modal Workflow (`src/components/modals/AddMemberModal.tsx`):
- Relationship Selection: Father, Mother, Son, Daughter, Brother, Sister, Spouse, Grandparent, Relative.
- Deduplication Engine: Real-time search suggests existing profiles to prevent duplicate entries in PostgreSQL.
- Optional Login Account: Can create a platform login account for the relative with email and password so they can log in to their own sanctuary portal.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. BACKEND VERIFICATION & DATABASE PERSISTENCE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.1. Memory Creation Endpoint (`POST /family/memories`):
- Controller: `src/family/family.controller.ts` -> `@Post('memories')`
- Service: `src/family/family.service.ts` -> `createMemory`
- Persistence: Creates a record in the `Memory` table with:
  - `title`: Provided title
  - `description`: Structured metadata (Category, Date, Location, Tagged, Privacy) + story body
  - `sharedBy`: Dynamic author name (`user.fullName || "Family Member"`)
  - `mediaUrl`: Serialized JSON array of all uploaded media URLs
  - `photoCount`: Total number of attached media items
  - `familyId`: Associated family sanctuary ID

4.2. Member Creation Endpoint (`POST /family/members`):
- Controller: `src/family/family.controller.ts` -> `@Post('members')`
- Service: `src/family/family.service.ts` -> `createMember`
- Persistence: Creates a record in the `FamilyMember` table and optionally generates a `User` login record and a `Relationship` link in PostgreSQL.

